+  <section id="code">
+    <p class="section-kicker">03 · Code</p>
+    <h2>The implementation keeps one orchestration path</h2>
+
+    <p>The code is easiest to read as five cooperating layers. The generated API client describes the wire contract. Settings choose the rollout route. One orchestration function owns the lifecycle. Poll helpers interpret remote state. Finally, both the one-shot command and wizard call that same orchestration function.</p>
+
+    <h3>1. Generate the contract instead of hand-writing HTTP</h3>
+    <p>The OpenAPI specification now includes submission and lookup routes for mirror requests. Ogen generates request types, response variants, state enums, client methods, and JSON codecs. Most of the PR’s raw line count is this mechanical boundary; the handwritten code consumes typed outcomes rather than parsing unstructured responses.</p>
+    <p>The consequential contract is small: submission can yield 202 with a request plus <code>Location</code>; polling yields pending, processing, succeeded, or failed; success contains a mirror result; failure contains a stable code, message, and retryability flag. See the <a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/1d65df23a2d6e584c3b7e536b13bda3bad5b3d66/internal/coreapi/spec/core.openapi.json#L10234-L10440">mirror-request routes in the pinned OpenAPI source</a>.</p>
+
+    <pre class="code"><span class="com">// Conceptual wire exchange</span>
+POST /api/v1/mirror-requests
+→ 202 Accepted
+→ Location: /api/v1/mirror-requests/7b88…
+
+GET /api/v1/mirror-requests/7b88…
+→ { <span class="key">"status"</span>: <span class="str">"succeeded"</span>, <span class="key">"result"</span>: { <span class="key">"mirror_id"</span>: <span class="str">"m_42"</span>, … } }</pre>
+
+    <h3>2. Route at the command boundary, then forget the flag</h3>
+    <p>The command loads normal layered settings and copies the boolean into <code>mirrorCreateOptions</code>. A settings-load error is deliberately non-fatal here because this control-plane command is exempt from the local <code>.entire</code> guard. After that boundary, callers pass one options value; they do not each reimplement rollout logic.</p>
+
+    <pre class="code">opts := mirrorCreateOptions{noWait: noWait, timeout: timeout}
+if settings, err := LoadEntireSettings(cmd.Context()); err == nil {
+    opts.async = settings.AsyncMirrorRequests
+}
+
+outcome, err := createAndAwaitMirror(ctx, client, owner, repo, cluster, opts)</pre>
+
+    <p>The setting itself is merged by the same scalar-setting machinery as other booleans. A local false can override a project true, which matters when one developer or test environment must remain on the legacy route. The behavior is pinned by the <a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/1d65df23a2d6e584c3b7e536b13bda3bad5b3d66/cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings_test.go#L667-L693">layered-settings test</a>.</p>
+
+    <h3>3. Extend the lifecycle without duplicating its second half</h3>
+    <p><a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/1d65df23a2d6e584c3b7e536b13bda3bad5b3d66/cmd/entire/cli/repo_mirror.go#L573-L660"><code>createAndAwaitMirror</code></a> is the center of the change. It selects only phase one: async submits and awaits a placement; sync calls the existing create method. Both branches then converge on the old clone-readiness poll and the same <code>--no-wait</code> behavior.</p>
+
+    <div class="figure">
+      <p class="figure-title">Control flow inside createAndAwaitMirror</p>
+      <p class="figure-note">The branch is narrow; placement results are normalized before common behavior resumes.</p>
+      <div class="split">
+        <div class="lane">
+          <span class="lane-label">Setting false · legacy</span>
+          <ol>
+            <li>Call synchronous <code>CreateMirror</code>.</li>
+            <li>Receive <code>CreatedMirror</code>.</li>
+            <li>Preserve created/existing output.</li>
+          </ol>
+        </div>
+        <div class="lane">
+          <span class="lane-label">Setting true · async</span>
+          <ol>
+            <li>Call <code>CreateMirrorRequest</code>.</li>
+            <li>Validate and poll <code>Location</code>.</li>
+            <li>Normalize success to <code>CreatedMirror</code>.</li>
+          </ol>
+        </div>
+      </div>
+      <div class="flow" style="margin-top: 14px">
+        <div class="node"><span class="n">Common result</span><code>placement + URLs</code></div>
+        <div class="arrow">→</div>
+        <div class="node"><span class="n">No wait?</span><code>return placed URL</code></div>
+        <div class="arrow">→</div>
+        <div class="node"><span class="n">Otherwise</span><code>awaitMirrorReady</code></div>
+        <div class="arrow">→</div>
+        <div class="node"><span class="n">Report</span><code>ready / failed / suspended</code></div>
+      </div>
+    </div>
+
+    <p>This convergence is the main maintainability win. The existing clone poll keeps its cadence, transient-error tolerance, and terminal-state handling. The new path adds a placement poll without creating a second version of everything that happens afterward.</p>
+
+    <h3>4. Make remote uncertainty bounded and explicit</h3>
+    <p><a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/1d65df23a2d6e584c3b7e536b13bda3bad5b3d66/cmd/entire/cli/repo_mirror_probe.go#L95-L210"><code>awaitMirrorPlacement</code></a> performs three jobs: validate the poll target, translate request states, and bound transient failures. Pending and processing continue. Succeeded must include a usable mirror result. Failed preserves the server’s code and message and adds retry advice only when the server marks the failure retryable.</p>
+    <p>Network errors and short-lived authorization misses are tolerated, but not forever. Fifteen consecutive errors at a two-second interval exhaust the tolerance. A successful response resets the streak. Context cancellation remains silent, while deadline errors identify whether time expired during submission, placement, or readiness so the user knows what completed.</p>
+
+    <div class="table-wrap">
+      <table>
+        <thead><tr><th>Observed state</th><th>CLI action</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
+        <tbody>
+          <tr><td>pending / processing</td><td>Continue polling every 2 s</td><td>The server still owns live work.</td></tr>
+          <tr><td>succeeded + result</td><td>Enter clone poll or honor <code>--no-wait</code></td><td>Placement now has a concrete URL.</td></tr>
+          <tr><td>failed</td><td>Return code + server detail; include retry advice when flagged</td><td>The durable request reached a terminal business failure.</td></tr>
+          <tr><td>transient GET error</td><td>Tolerate up to 15 consecutive failures</td><td>Routing and authorization can be briefly stale.</td></tr>
+          <tr><td>deadline exceeded</td><td>Name the phase that timed out</td><td>A generic timeout would hide whether submission succeeded.</td></tr>
+        </tbody>
+      </table>
+    </div>
+
+    <h3>5. Keep cross-jurisdiction repair below the orchestration</h3>
+    <p>The request poller should not need to understand 421 responses, home-core discovery, or token exchange. The existing transport already owns those concerns. The PR extends that layer to canonicalize a successful async submission’s <code>Location</code> against the final request URL. That makes the generated response safe for ordinary callers to follow and keeps jurisdiction logic out of mirror orchestration.</p>
+    <p>The behavior is visible in <a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/1d65df23a2d6e584c3b7e536b13bda3bad5b3d66/internal/coreapi/cross_juris_transport.go#L304-L326">the transport’s narrow canonicalization hook</a> and its adjacent focused test.</p>
+
+    <h3>6. Make one-shot and wizard differ only in presentation</h3>
+    <p>The positional command creates one target and shows one spinner. The wizard may create several repository/region targets concurrently, with a limit of eight, and reports failures independently. Both now pass the same options into <code>createAndAwaitMirror</code>. The wizard installs a per-target phase callback, but it does not own a separate async implementation.</p>
+    <p>This shared path is tested in layers: focused tests exercise submission, status handling, Location validation, timeout and cancellation, cross-jurisdiction retry, settings selection, and output wording; a wizard test confirms concurrency remains bounded and one target’s failure does not cancel the rest. The main matrix lives in <a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/1d65df23a2d6e584c3b7e536b13bda3bad5b3d66/cmd/entire/cli/repo_mirror_request_test.go">the async mirror request test file</a>.</p>
+
+    <div class="callout good">
+      <span class="callout-label">Verification evidence</span>
+      <p>The branch passed formatting, lint with zero issues, the race-enabled integration suite, 56 Vogon canaries, and 4 Roger canaries. Current-head Bugbot, Copilot, and Entire review findings were clean when the review cycle settled.</p>
+    </div>
+
+    <h3>How the commits form independent review slices</h3>
+    <p>The branch history mirrors the architecture: generated contract first, transport behavior next, then rollout configuration, shared runtime behavior, feedback corrections, precise timeout wording, and a final behavior-preserving simplification.</p>
+
+    <div class="commit-stack">
+      <div class="commit"><a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/f35ce74b6a1b1328971131ced6382a75f5b952e7">f35ce74b6a</a><p><strong>Generate the mirror-request API client.</strong> Establishes typed wire shapes from OpenAPI.</p></div>
+      <div class="commit"><a href="https://github.com/entireio/cli/commit/d3629367921290a37166061fe51bf250f196c003">d362936792</a><p><strong>Canonicalize request locations.</strong> Keeps cross-jurisdiction polling on the effective home core.</p></div>
